# Main list tables

Any **main list** that can show more than ~10 rows (surveys, users, groups, questions, catalogs, logs, etc.) must match the user-management table pattern.

## Required

- Hide/show **filters** via `TableOptionsMenu` (`Show filters`)
- **Column visibility** via `useColumnVisibility` + `TableOptionsMenu`
- Sortable headers where the data supports it
- Page size (10/25/50/100) and Previous/Next
- Prefer API `page`, `limit`, `sort`, `order`, and filter query params with `{ items, pagination, sort }`. If the endpoint is not paginated yet, filter/sort/page on the client and still show the same toolbar.
- Row actions are icon buttons (`AccessIconButton` / `AccessIconLink`), not text links
- `overflow-x-auto` so the table works on small screens; keep action icons always visible on touch (`TableActionRow`)

```tsx
<TableOptionsMenu
  columns={columns}
  isVisible={isVisible}
  toggle={toggle}
  showFilters={showFilters}
  onToggleFilters={() => setShowFilters((prev) => !prev)}
/>
```

## Do not

- Ship a bare 10+ row table with no filters, sort, pagination, or column picker
- Use this pattern for tiny summary tables (a handful of fixed rows)
